From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The HM cut-in's sprites drawn by the 3DS till its band's window goes (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

As the cut-in ends it deletes its sprites, puts BG3 back (cleared) and,
a game frame later, takes its window away. The DS shows the last of the
sprites in the band's 16 lines till then. The 3DS's compositor stopped
drawing the sprites (NitroPort_SetFieldCells FALSE) as they were
deleted, so those two frames' pictures had them drawn in, which isn't
a band the compositor can draw: the band jumped back open to 16 lines,
the DS's own, and its close at 60 frames a second wasn't seen through.
The compositor now draws them till the window goes (and, if the cut-in
is ended before that, as it's freed).

---
diff --git a/src/overlay006/hm_cut_in.c b/src/overlay006/hm_cut_in.c
index 2e28ba40..28828307 100644
--- a/src/overlay006/hm_cut_in.c
+++ b/src/overlay006/hm_cut_in.c
@@ -295,6 +295,9 @@ static void CutIn_UnloadPokemonSpriteResources(HMCutIn *cutIn);
 static void CutIn_ClearTileMapBG3(BgConfig *bgConfig);
 static void CutIn_DeleteSpriteResources(HMCutIn *cutIn);
 static void CutIn_UpdateSpriteList(HMCutIn *cutIn);
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+static void CutIn_PortFieldCellsOff(void);
+#endif
 
 // Cut-In window
 static void CutIn_InitWindow(HMCutIn *cutIn);
@@ -1096,6 +1099,9 @@ static HMCutIn *CreateHMCutIn(FieldSystem *fieldSystem)
 
 static void FreeHMCutIn(HMCutIn *cutIn)
 {
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    CutIn_PortFieldCellsOff(); // (if it ended before its window did)
+#endif
     Heap_Free(cutIn);
 }
 
@@ -1376,6 +1382,9 @@ static BOOL HMCutIn_DeleteSprites(HMCutIn *cutIn)
 
 static BOOL HMCutIn_WindowTaskDone(HMCutIn *cutIn)
 {
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    CutIn_PortFieldCellsOff();
+#endif
     CutIn_DeleteWindowTask(cutIn);
     cutIn->state++;
     return FALSE;
@@ -1743,6 +1752,17 @@ extern void NitroPort_RepeatingBg(int bg, int on);
 // the DS's sprites' x does (past 256 + its band, on the left side).
 extern void NitroPort_SetFieldCells(int on);
 
+// The sprites still drawn by the 3DS's compositor (NitroPort_SetFieldCells
+// FALSE ends that too) until the band's window goes, a game frame after its
+// sprites are deleted: the DS shows the last of them in the band's 16 lines
+// till then. Ended with the sprites, those frames were the 2D's own band,
+// drawn in the picture: the band jumped back open to 16 lines and stopped
+// there, its close at 60 frames a second not seen through (2026-11-03).
+static void CutIn_PortFieldCellsOff(void)
+{
+    NitroPort_SetFieldCells(FALSE);
+}
+
 // The band beside the DS's screen: three more rings each side, fading on
 // (two darker shades of the band's colour), as drawn for the wider screen
 // (2026-10-30). Made here from the game's own band: its middle ring's
@@ -2048,7 +2068,6 @@ static void CutIn_DeleteSprites(HMCutIn *cutIn)
     CutIn_ClearTileMapBG3(cutIn->fieldSystem->bgConfig);
 #ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
     NitroPort_RepeatingBg(3, FALSE);
-    NitroPort_SetFieldCells(FALSE);
 #endif
     CutIn_DeleteSpriteResources(cutIn);
 
-- 
